1
00:00:00,178 --> 00:00:03,138
...I'm a bit of a self-taught expert.

2
00:00:04,683 --> 00:00:08,023
Howard, if I were to ask Leslie Winkle out,
it would just be for dinner.

3
00:00:08,186 --> 00:00:12,026
I'm not gonna walk into the lab,
ask her to strip naked and dance for me.

4
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:14,440
(Howard:)Oh, then you're probably okay.

5
00:00:18,155 --> 00:00:20,115
- Hello, Leslie.
- Hi, Leonard.

6
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:22,412
- I'd like to propose an experiment...
- Goggles.

7
00:00:22,576 --> 00:00:23,866
(Howard:)Right.

8
00:00:25,954 --> 00:00:28,994
(Leonard:)- I would like to propose an experiment.
- Hang on.

9
00:00:29,166 --> 00:00:32,546
(Lesley:)I'm trying to see how long it takes
a 500-kilowatt oxygen-iodine laser...

10
00:00:32,711 --> 00:00:34,841
...to heat up my cup of noodles.

11
00:00:35,922 --> 00:00:38,762
(Leonard:)I've done it.
About two seconds, 2.6 for minestrone.

12
00:00:40,761 --> 00:00:42,971
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

13
00:00:45,515 --> 00:00:48,725
(Leonard:)Anyway, I was thinking more
of a biosocial exploration...

14
00:00:48,894 --> 00:00:50,774
(Leonard:)...with a neurochemical overlay.

15
00:00:52,439 --> 00:00:54,779
(Lesley:)Wait, are you asking me out?

16
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:58,110
I was going to characterize it
as the modification...

17
00:00:58,278 --> 00:01:02,408
(Leonard:)...of our colleague/friendship paradigm
with the addition of a date-like component.

